{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>How shall I curse — El has not cursed.</b> When they were worthy of being cursed, they were not cursed — when their father mentioned their sin, ״כִּי בְאַפָּם הָרְגוּ אִישׁ״, he cursed only their anger, as it says ״אָרוּר אַפָּם״ (Genesis 49); when their father came with deception to his father he was worthy of being cursed — what is said there? ״גַּם בָּרוּךְ יִהְיֶה״ (ibid. 27). Of those who bless it says ״אֵלֶּה יַעַמְדוּ לְבָרֵךְ אֶת הָעָם״; of those who curse it does not say וְאֵלֶּה יַעַמְדוּ לְקַלֵּל אֶת הָעָם, but rather ״וְאֵלֶּה יַעַמְדוּ עַל הַקְּלָלָה״ (Deuteronomy 27) — He did not wish to mention the name קְלָלָה upon them (Tanchuma)." "<b>nor is YHWH wrathful.</b> I have no power except that I know how to pinpoint the moment when the Holy One, blessed be He, is wrathful — and He was not wrathful all these days that I have come to you. And this is what is said (Micah 6) ״עַמִּי זְכָר נָא מַה יָּעַץ״ etc., ״וּמֶה עָנָה אֹתוֹ בִלְעָם״ etc., ״לְמַעַן דַּעַת צִדְקוֹת ה׳״ (Sanhedrin 105)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:26.262310945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}